{"explanation":"Updates Encryptor.encryptToken to use the coordinated current-lifecycle Cipher preparation and encryption entry points while preserving its public signature and successful map-return behavior. InvalidAlgorithmParameterException from the package-private preparation API is translated into the already-declared InvalidKeyException rather than being left unreported.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher(SecretKey) is implemented by the coordinated EncryptedKey edit so AndroidKeyStore keys configured for randomized encryption let the provider generate the fresh retained GCM nonce rather than rejecting a caller-supplied nonce.","The existing AndroidKeyStore alias "masterKey" remains the approved wrapping-key alias for this caller; no alias or persisted-record-format migration is introduced in this file.","This class has no decryption entry point, so legacy-versus-current record key selection through EncryptedKey.usesCurrentWrappingKey() is applicable to the coordinated decryption owners, not to encryptToken."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {
        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();

        Key mk = null;
        try {
            mk = mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Exception", e);
        }

        // Encrypt token key
        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt((SecretKey) mk, key);

        data.put("key", ekc);
        return data;
    }","edit_kind":"method","corrected_code":"    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {
        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();

        Key mk = null;
        try {
            mk = mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Exception", e);
        }

        // Encrypt token key
        javax.crypto.Cipher encryptionCipher;
        try {
            encryptionCipher = EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher((SecretKey) mk);
        } catch (java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException e) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Unable to prepare AndroidKeyStore encryption", e);
        }
        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionCipher, key);

        data.put("key", ekc);
        return data;
    }","reason":"Uses the coordinated prepared-Cipher API so EncryptedKey retains provider-generated AES-GCM parameters for current records. The catch preserves encryptToken's existing checked-exception contract and propagates preparation failure as its already-declared InvalidKeyException." ,"symbol":"Encryptor.encryptToken"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["encryptToken retains its public signature and returns a map containing the encrypted token under "key" on successful AndroidKeyStore encryption.","encryptToken obtains the existing MASTER AndroidKeyStore wrapping key and passes it to EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher before invoking EncryptedKey.encrypt(Cipher, SecretKey)."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey must provide package-private prepareEncryptionCipher(SecretKey) and package-private encrypt(Cipher, SecretKey) as specified by the coordinated contract.","EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher must support AndroidKeyStore randomized-encryption keys by allowing the provider to generate the fresh GCM nonce and retained parameters."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","required_tests":["The coordinated EncryptedKey instrumentation tests must exercise Encryptor.encryptToken with the AndroidKeyStore MASTER alias and verify successful encryption/decryption.","The coordinated tests must verify repeated current-lifecycle encryption retains distinct provider-generated GCM nonces and that legacy records remain decryptable through their legacy resolution path."]}
